{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy gives priority to forward progress in clear conditions, uses short directed turns for side/front obstacles, allows one brief backward escape only from a dedicated front-obstacle recovery state, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path. Action states are one-shot, and uncontrollable events are total in every specification state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in G",
    "Use specification automata to bind sensor outcomes to exactly one recovery/exploration action per policy state while keeping obstacle handling safe and progress-oriented"
  ],
